Information related to cluster is stored in the kube/config 
# ~/.kube/config
1. first we should generate the users private key 
#openssl genrsa -out pavan.key 2048
then we must create a certificate signing request for the user with the key 
this command generate certifcate signning request 
#openssl req -new pavan.key  -out pavan.csr -subj "/CN=pavan/O=dev/O=example.org
CN stands for common name , it act like username 
O act like group name , we can give multiple groups to the current user 
-out pavan.csr = storing certificate signing request to the current folder 

Now the private key and certificate siging request are ready 
#ls | grep pavan 
Now this certificate siging request must be signed by the certificate authority 
they can get the certificate authority details from kubeconfig file 

to sign it , to generate this command

#openssl x509 -req -CA ~/.minikube/ca.crt -CAkey ~/.minikube/ca.key -CAcreateserial -days 730 -in pavan.csr  -out pavan.crt

in Kube/config file 
cluster:
  certificate-authority:/Users/pavan.elthepu/.minikube/ca.crt


