we should try to give permisions to the users 
in kubernate , we can give the permisions to a user with roles and rolebinding 
this is simple role monifiest file 
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata;
  name: pod-reader
rules:
  - apiGroup: [""] #"" indicates the core API group 
    verbs: ["get","watch","list"]
    resources: ["pods","pods/log"]

#kubectl apply -f role.yaml

Now User and ROle both are ready , now connect bothso that user will be having these permissions 
In ROleBinding we connect both subject and Role 
this subject can be user or usergroup or even a service account 
and role we defined what we can access and what we cannot access when we attach the subject and roll with RoleBinding we are attaching the permissions to the user 


Note: RollBinding is nothing but connecting a user to a role 
